<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pokhran</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pokhran is a town in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thar-desert">Thar Desert</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajasthan">Rajasthan</a>, in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, near which lies the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indian-army">Indian Army</a>'s test range. India carried out its first nuclear test there on 18 May 1974, code-named Smiling Buddha, and five further tests in May 1998, after which it declared itself a nuclear-weapon state; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pakistan">Pakistan</a> answered with its own tests weeks later.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pokhran.jpg" alt="Pokhran" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Archan dave · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pokhran_Fort.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
